l adopted resolution 2739 (2024) by 12 votes in favour, with Algeria, China, and the Russian Federation abstaining. Draft S/2024/500, sponsored by the United States and Japan, extended the Secretary-General's reporting deadline to 15 January 2025 to monitor Houthi attacks on commerce. The sponsors argued this extension ensures accurate data tracking, while Algeria abstained citing concerns over the implementation of resolution 2722 and potential misuse of self-defence provisions. Although both the sponsors and Algeria agreed on the reporting extension, a critical difference persisted regarding the demand that the Houthis cease attacks on merchant vessels; Algeria opposed this specific demand, whereas the sponsors insisted upon it. No military authorization was added to the adopted text.", "input_tokens": 542, "output_tokens": 180, "termination": "complete"}}
